# Manifests, sidecars and golden vectors commit to the SHA-256 of file bytes, so a checkout
# that rewrites line endings changes what the protocol pins. With core.autocrlf=true and no
# .gitattributes, a clone on Windows rewrites line endings, and every digest over those files
# stops matching the bytes that were committed. Normalizing to LF makes the working tree
# identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: any translation here corrupts the artifact.
*.zip binary
*.bin binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
